  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reverse Trade Mission - U.S.-Brazil Aviation Partnership Phase IV Initiative, through American Association of Airport Executives</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The U.S.-Brazil Aviation Partnership Phase IV Initiative seeks to expand commercial opportunities in Brazil for the U.S. aviation industry through the sharing of experiences, best practices and technology solutions. The Airport Infrastructure Track of Phase IV of this Partnership is proposed to be carried out through a program of separate and distinct activities, including two reverse trade missions, two workshops and three technical webinars. The Phase IV Initiative would commence in late summer 2019 and would be carried out over a period of approximately 18 months.</narrative>
  </description>
